The user-facing symptom is confined to the trip-search path. Requests through `ts-ui-dashboard` to `/api/v1/travelservice/trips/left` and the travel-plan endpoints take 20–130s and return errors, while the other dashboard paths stay near their normal latency (about 70ms). The one fault is a sustained network partition on the `ts-seat-service` → `ts-order-service` connection. Seat's ticket-order POSTs never reach order-service and time out. The slowness then climbs the call chain from seat to travel to route-plan to travel-plan to the dashboard. Routing this fault to `ts-seat-service` follows the schema's convention of naming the caller end. Restarts, pod-level network errors, and CPU/memory limits show nothing abnormal, so resource exhaustion is ruled out.
